Reuse of this material is NOT cleared. The repository is private for that reason.

Source of the text: Narodne novine (https://narodne-novine.nn.hr), the official gazette of the Republic of Croatia,
published by Narodne novine d.d., Zagreb. The text of the Constitution of the Republic of Croatia (NN 56/1990 and its
changes), its consolidated texts (NN 8/1998, 124/2000, 41/2001, 55/2001, 85/2010) and the Constitutional Court
decision NN 5/2014 no. 93 was read from the public pages, one request at a time and at no more than three requests
per second, as the page "Pristup podatcima" asks. Attribution: "Narodne novine d.d., narodne-novine.nn.hr".

What Narodne novine's terms of use say ("Opći uvjeti korištenja", under "Zaštita autorskog prava"), in the original:

    Svi sadržaji objavljeni na ovim internetskim stranicama zaštićeni su autorskim pravom i mogu se koristiti samo
    pod uvjetima propisanima Zakonom.

("All content published on these web pages is protected by copyright and may be used only under the conditions
prescribed by law.") The same terms say that Narodne novine d.d. take reasonable care that the information is complete
and accurate but are not liable for inaccuracy or incompleteness. The "Pristup podatcima" page says that use of the
online database is "dostupno svima, anonimno i besplatno" (available to everyone, anonymously and free of charge) and
invites crawlers and scripts to index and use the content (sitemaps, ELI metadata, an API), at no more than three
requests per second. It states no licence for copying or republishing the texts.

Whether, and on what conditions, the text of the Constitution or of a gazette page may be copied and republished is
therefore unclear to us. We have not decided it and have not asked Narodne novine d.d. Until that is settled the
repository stays private and no licence is granted for the law text. This is not legal advice.

zakon.hr (a private, unofficial site with consolidated versions) was not used as a source of text; its terms forbid
automated extraction. Its list of amending acts was used only as a pointer to which Narodne novine issues to read, as
REPRODUCE.md says.

Everything that is not law text (the history as commits, the commit messages, the tools) was made by Lexifina; no
licence is granted for it either until the question above is settled.
